Policy definitions for document roles:

- H_AND_P: a history and physical examination note. Titles vary widely in
  abbreviation and formatting, and may carry prefixes or suffixes. A retained
  or older H&P is still an H&P; being out of date is handled elsewhere. A
  document that merely references an H&P performed elsewhere is not one.
- SURGICAL_CONSENT: a consent document for the surgical procedure itself.
- ANTICOAG_PLAN: a perioperative anticoagulation management plan.
- OTHER: anything else.

`signed` applies only to SURGICAL_CONSENT: true if the text clearly indicates a
signature, false if it clearly indicates none, null if undeterminable.
`plan_is_clear` applies only to ANTICOAG_PLAN: true only if the text says how
the medication is actually managed around the procedure.

